# /etc/rc.local -- your own commands, run by /etc/rc at the end of the
# boot, after the network, the firewall and the services are up.  Try a
# command at the shell first; when it does what you want, add it here and
# run saveconfig: from the next boot on, it is part of the router's setup.
# A command that fails prints its error on the console; the rest still runs.
#
# Examples (see chapter 3 of the docs):
#
# A static route to a network behind another router on the LAN:
#	route add -net 10.20.0.0/16 192.168.77.254
#
# Port 4 on its own network, VLAN 10 (the switch table first, then the
# router's interface on it):
#	sysctl -w hw.qcomess0.vlans="1:1,2,5 2:3 10:4"
#	ifconfig vlan10 create
#	ifconfig vlan10 vlan 10 vlanif qcomedma0
#	ifconfig vlan10 inet 192.168.10.1/24 up
